# Independent Plan Browser toolbar controls

Separate the graph and contextual-help controls so interaction feedback and actions cannot leak between them.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Graph and help are implemented as separate controls rather than a shared interactive container.
- [ ] Tapping or pressing Graph does not animate, bounce, highlight, or invoke Help.
- [ ] Tapping or pressing Help does not animate, bounce, highlight, or invoke Graph.
- [ ] Each control retains an adequate, non-overlapping tap target and accessible label.
- [ ] Graph navigation behavior remains consistent with the currently implemented SCR-003 scope.
- [ ] Automated interaction coverage compiles for both directions.
- [ ] Focused UI checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- This supersedes the earlier hit-target-only interpretation in TASK-011; pressed-state independence is required as well.
